sudo: no RTLD_NEXT lookups under Fil-C

Nixpkgs 26.11's sudo carries the CVE-2026-96512 fix, which makes sudo call
unsetenv("TZ") at startup. sudo's own unsetenv() hook looks up the libc one
with dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, ...), and Fil-C's dlsym() stops the program on
RTLD_NEXT ("cannot access pointer with null object" in zsys_dlsym), so
every sudo invocation died. sudo already supports platforms without
RTLD_NEXT: sudo_dso_findsym() returns NULL, and the putenv, setenv and
unsetenv hooks use sudo's replacements instead. Take that branch under
Fil-C.

--- a/lib/util/sudo_dso.c
+++ b/lib/util/sudo_dso.c
@@ -339,7 +339,8 @@
      * Not all implementations support the special handles.
      */
     if (handle == SUDO_DSO_NEXT) {
-# ifdef RTLD_NEXT
+	/* Fil-C's dlsym() stops the program on RTLD_NEXT. */
+# if defined(RTLD_NEXT) && !defined(__FILC__)
 	handle = RTLD_NEXT;
 # else
 	errno = ENOENT;
